# {%.Name%}

{%if eq .UI "live"%}A web app built with [Vuka](https://vuka-lang.github.io/): live pages styled
with Tailwind{%else if eq .UI "templ"%}A web app built with [Vuka](https://vuka-lang.github.io/): templ views
styled with Tailwind{%else%}A JSON API built with [Vuka](https://vuka-lang.github.io/){%end%}{%if .Auth%}, sign-in with sessions kept in the database{%end%}{%if ne .DB "none"%}, migrations
applied when it starts{%end%}.

## Run it

```sh
vuka run -watch .      # http://localhost:8080; rebuilt on every save
vuka test ./...
```
{%- if .Auth%}

Sign in as the admin in `.env` (`ADMIN_EMAIL`, `ADMIN_PASSWORD`). The app
creates that user when it starts and no user has the email yet; changing
the values later changes nothing.
{%- end%}
{%- if or (eq .DB "postgres") (eq .DB "mysql")%}

Create the database `DATABASE_URL` names in `.env` first. The tests run on
SQLite and need no server.
{%- end%}
{%- if .Pages%}

The Tailwind CLI builds the stylesheet (`brew install tailwindcss`, or
`npm i -D @tailwindcss/cli`); without it the pages run unstyled.
{%- end%}
{%- if ne .Frontend "none"%}

`vuka run` also starts the frontend's Vite dev server (it installs the
dependencies the first time from `frontend/package-lock.json`; adding
packages needs npm 11 or newer), and
the app serves the frontend at [/app](http://localhost:8080/app/).
{%- end%}
{%- if .Islands%}

The sample Vue island at [/island](http://localhost:8080/island) is built from
`web/`, a Vite project with Nuxt UI. Install its dependencies once from the
lockfile (Node.js 20+; adding packages needs npm 11 or newer); then `vuka
run`/`vuka build` compiles the island through Vite and serves
(or embeds) it. The Nuxt UI component in `web/islands/Counter.vue` resolves and
styles itself out of the box.

```sh
(cd web && npm ci)
```
{%- end%}

