## Grow it

A module is the unit of growth: its model, service, {%if eq .UI "templ"%}page{%else if not .Pages%}routes{%end%}{%if ne .UI "live"%} {%end%}and test in
`modules/<name>/`{%if eq .UI "live"%}, its page in `pages/<name>/`{%end%}, its table in a migration.

```sh
vuka add module notes
```

writes `modules/notes/` (a `Note` model, a `Notes` service, {%if eq .UI "templ"%}a page at
`/notes` linked in the navigation, {%else if not .Pages%}`/api/notes` routes, {%end%}a test){%if eq .UI "live"%}, its page
`pages/notes/index.vuka.html` at `/notes`, linked in the navigation{%end%}, a migration making the
`notes` table, and the import in `main.vuka` that registers its service.
Rename fields, add some: it's yours.

**Changing the schema.** Edit a model, then write the migration:

```sh
go tool orm makemigrations      # DATABASE_URL (.env) says the dialect
```

Read the file it writes in `migrations/` and commit it. The app applies
pending migrations when it starts; `go tool orm showmigrations` lists them
and `go tool orm migrate` applies them without starting the app.
{%- end%}
{%- if .Pages%}

**A page.** {%if eq .UI "live"%}A `.vuka.html` file under `pages/` is a page, its path its
URL: `pages/reports/[id].vuka.html` is `/reports/{id}`, its struct's `ID`
field the parameter. The struct and its methods sit above the markup; one
embedding `ui.Live` is live, its state on the server and the page changed
in place on each event, and `@ui.Mount` marks the method that loads it.
`pages/_layout.vuka.html` is the document around every page. Wrap a page
in `layouts.App`, and add `layouts.Nav(layouts.Link{…})` to link it;
`vuka add page /path` writes one, and `vuka routes` lists them.{%else%}A function with `@web.Get("/path")` and `@web.Template("view.templ")`
is a page: the templ component beside it renders its result. Wrap it in
`layouts.App`, and add `layouts.Nav(layouts.Link{…})` to link it.{%end%}

**A component.** A `components/*.vuka.html` file is a component every page
can use: `<components.Card title="…">…</components.Card>`{%if eq .UI "templ"%}, or
`@components.Card{Title: "…"}` from templ{%end%}. `vuka add component Name`
writes one: its struct (the props, its exported fields) above its markup.
{%- end%}
{%- if .Auth%}

## Sign-in

`auth.Module` in `main.vuka` guards every route{%if .Pages%}, page and live event{%end%}: each
needs a sign-in unless marked `@auth.Public`, and `@auth.Requires("perm")`
asks for a permission. Roles grant permissions (`users.Roles`: an admin
has every one, a member `users.read`). {%if .Pages%}The sign-in page posts to
`/auth/login`; "remember me" keeps a sign-in for two weeks, else it ends with
the browser session.{%end%} APIs take a bearer token from `POST /auth/token`.
{%- end%}
{%- if .Mail%}

## Mail

`MAIL_DRIVER=log` prints messages instead of sending them (the development
toolbar's Mail panel shows them). In production set `MAIL_DRIVER=smtp`
and `MAIL_HOST`, `MAIL_PORT`, `MAIL_USERNAME`, `MAIL_PASSWORD`.
{%- end%}

## Ship it

```sh
vuka build -o {%.Slug%} .   # one binary{%if .Pages%}: pages, styles{%end%}{%if ne .Frontend "none"%}, the frontend{%end%} and all
```

Run it with real environment variables in place of `.env` (see
`.env.example`){%if eq .DB "sqlite"%}; the SQLite file lives in `data/`, so keep that directory
on a disk that persists{%end%}.
